<body class="article">
<div id="header">
<h1>Extensions</h1>
</div>
<div id="content">
<div id="preamble">
<div class="sectionbody">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Extensions are central to the success of AsciiDoc because they open up the language to new use cases.
Asciidoctor provides an {url-api-gems}/asciidoctor/{release-version}/Asciidoctor/Extensions[extension API^] that offers a superset of extension points.
As a result, extensions in Asciidoctor are easy to write, powerful, and simple to distribute.</p>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Asciidoctor also allows extensions to be written using the full power of a programming language (whether it be Ruby, Java, Groovy or JavaScript).
You don&#8217;t have to shave yaks to get the functionality you want, and you can distribute the extension using de facto standard packaging mechanisms like gems or JARs.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sect1">
<h2 id="_available_extension_points">Available extension points</h2>
<div class="sectionbody">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Asciidoctor provides the following extension points:</p>
</div>
<div class="dlist">
<dl>
<dt class="hdlist1">Preprocessor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Processes the raw source lines before they are passed to the parser.
See <a href="preprocessor.html">preprocessor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Tree processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Processes the <span class="class">Asciidoctor::Document</span> (AST) once parsing is complete.
See <a href="tree-processor.html">tree-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Postprocessor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Processes the output after the document has been converted, but before it&#8217;s written to disk.
See <a href="postprocessor.html">postprocessor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Docinfo Processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Adds additional content to the header or footer regions of the generated document.
See <a href="docinfo-processor.html">docinfo-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Block processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Processes a block of content marked with a custom block style (e.g., <code>[custom]</code>).
See <a href="block-processor.html">block-processor.html</a> and <a href="compound-block-processor.html">compound-block-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Block macro processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Registers a custom block macro and processes it (e.g., <code>gist::12345[]</code>).
See <a href="block-macro-processor.html">block-macro-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Inline macro processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Registers a custom inline macro and processes it (e.g., <code>btn:[Save]</code>).
See <a href="inline-macro-processor.html">inline-macro-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
<dt class="hdlist1">Include processor</dt>
<dd>
<p>Processes the <code>include::&lt;filename&gt;[]</code> directive.
See <a href="include-processor.html">include-processor.html</a>.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>There are additional extension examples in the <a href="https://github.com/asciidoctor/asciidoctor-extensions-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Asciidoctor extensions lab</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
